  "emission": {
    "tool_use_progress": "pOs f(b): for every item the tool yields with b.type===\"progress\" and b.data.type!==\"tool_heartbeat\", during call, before tengu_tool_use_success/error of the same call; messageID = yt(assistantMessage.message.id) (runToolUse Ux: a=t.message.id), toolName = fr(tool.name), isMcp = tool.isMcp ?? false, queryChainId/queryDepth = toolUseContext.queryTracking, mcpServerType/mcpServerBaseUrl only for connected MCP servers, requestId = yt(assistantMessage.requestId) when defined (Ux: l=t.requestId), Aw(name, mcpNameLoggable) and mcpInfo.pluginTelemetry spreads (empty for the owned non-MCP tools)",
    "task_output_waiting_for_task": "TaskOutput call: block mode only, after the task lookup (validateInput already rejected unknown ids) and before await aps(...), whether or not the task is already terminal: one {type:\"progress\", toolUseID:`task-output-waiting-${Date.now()}`, data:{type:\"waiting_for_task\", taskDescription, taskType}} item; non-block calls yield none",
    "cache_eviction_hint_subagent_end": "DMt(messages, agentId, ctx, {suppressTelemetry}) agent finalize when !suppressTelemetry: after D(\"tengu_agent_tool_completed\") and xl(\"subagent_completed\"), z = vb(messages).requestId (last assistant message); emitted only when z is defined: {scope:\"subagent_end\", last_request_id: yt(z)}",
    "cache_eviction_hint_other_scopes": "scope \"session_end\" (shutdown, WKe() last request id) and \"conversation_clear\" (/clear, _403.js) are process-level moments the gateway does not own",
    "feature_bad": "gOs call catch: oe=FXe(re) (abort error), Se=Tz(abortSignal); when !Se&&!oe: {code,isSad}=BUr(re); isSad => te(f,code) (tengu_feature_sad); else me(...) then J(f,code) => tengu_feature_bad {feature_name:f, error_code:code} immediately before D(\"tengu_tool_use_error\"); f = FUr(tool.name, mcpInfo) = toolFeature(name). BUr tail: plain Error/TypeError (name not in _Wt, no transport code) => {code:\"tool_call_threw\", isSad:false}. The outer runToolUse catch (permission/hook phase) uses the constant \"tool_unexpected_error\" instead",
    "resume_print": "print / sdk_url lane: first statement inside the `if(r.resume){... try{` block, before the session lookup (Fm/BP), before clearSessionCaches and hydration; empty native object (logger prefix only); tengu_session_resumed(print, success) is emitted later in the same try block after Hp() hydration, so tengu_resume_print always precedes it under the same r.resume condition"
  },
